{"sourceSha256": "1fd96c26a82b16ceb1ef7171034d6b84334becc779070f644a0b5e2f10bbf5ef", "text": "Question 6 According to the procedure, when inserting a catheter clinicians should\n\nNot yet answered\n\nSelect one:\nMarked out of 1.00\n\nA. only use a catheter once.\n\\P Flag question\n\nB. carefully follow all guidelines.\n\nC. ensure the patient isn’t left alone.\n\nInformation\n\nP Flag question\n\nCatheter Insertion Procedure\n\nWhere possible, use a two clinician buddy system to carry out the procedure. The patient's ethical,\nreligious and cultural beliefs and personal history should be considered when appointing clinicians to\nperform a catheterisation. A chaperone may also be required to observe the procedure.\n\nIt is recommended that the patient's genital area be washed with soap and water prior to\ncatheterisation. If unable to insert a catheter after two attempts (includes changing to a different\ncatheter size), seek further assistance from a senior clinician. A new catheter should be used for each\nattempt.\n\nTesting of the catheter balloon prior to insertion may compromise the integrity of some catheters.\nRefer to manufacturer's instructions to see if pre-insertion testing is required.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Question 6 According to the procedure, when inserting a catheter clinicians should\n\nNot yet answered\n\nSelect one:\nMarked out of 1.00\n\nA. only use a catheter once.\n\\P Flag question\n\nB. carefully follow all guidelines.\n\nC. ensure the patient isn’t left alone.\n\nInformation\n\nP Flag question\n\nCatheter Insertion Procedure\n\nWhere possible, use a two clinician buddy system to carry out the procedure. The patient's ethical,\nreligious and cultural beliefs and personal history should be considered when appointing clinicians to\nperform a catheterisation. A chaperone may also be required to observe the procedure.\n\nIt is recommended that the patient's genital area be washed with soap and water prior to\ncatheterisation. If un